# Allow-list: exclude everything, then re-include what the image needs.
# Keeping this an allow-list means repo housekeeping files (README, LICENSE,
# workflows, git metadata) can never leak into the public web root, and a newly
# added file cannot sneak into the image by accident.
*

# The site
!index.html

# The self-hosted typeface — the .woff2 only. OFL.txt, subset.sh and
# check-coverage.py belong to the repository, not to the web root; the CI smoke
# test fetches the font over HTTP, so an image that lost it fails the build
# rather than falling back to a system face in silence.
!fonts/*.woff2

# Build inputs that are not published
!docker/
